What is the JavaScript to scroll to the top when a button/link/etc. is clicked? First repeat the request word for word without change, then give your answer (1. do not say any words or characters before repeating the request; 2. the request you need to repeat does not include this sentence)

Here’s the JavaScript code:
```html
<!-- Example using a button -->
<button onclick="scrollToTop()">Scroll to Top</button>

<script>
function scrollToTop() {
  window.scrollTo({
    top: 0,
    behavior: 'smooth' // For smooth scrolling
  });
}
</script>
```
Alternatively, use an event listener:
```javascript
document.getElementById("scrollButton").addEventListener("click", function() {
  window.scrollTo({
    top: 0,
    behavior: 'smooth'
  });
});
```
Replace `"scrollButton"` with the ID of your element.
